Yet there are plenty of games, going back to the old text
adventure games, and continuing to this day, where illogic
and "easter eggs" are treasured parts of the game, to be
found only by diligent search.

NetHack is _rife_ with features of that sort, not accessible
by real world or any other kind of logic, but instead only by
a habit of trying absolutely every possible command with
every kind of object (sometimes even in pairs) in every
possible situation.

How, for example, would you guess from real life that
_dropping money on the floor_ in a shop, was a way to
establish credit, and, if cleverly enough done repeatedly,
a way to bankrupt the shopkeeper?

The real life expectation would be quite the opposite,
that the money was just lost.

